    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Roots of a Cubic Equation With Complex Roots Given One Complex Root",
    "problem": "Find all of the solutions to ${x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20=0$ given that $x=3-\\text{i}$ is a solution.",
    "worked_solution": "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20.$ \n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=3-\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}}=3+\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$(x-(3-\\text{i}))(x-(3+\\text{i}))$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(3-\\text{i}))(x-(3+\\text{i})) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(3-\\text{i}+(3+\\text{i)})x+(3-\\text{i})(3+\\text{i}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x+({3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x+10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-6x+10$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+2 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-6x+10\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-12x+20 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-12x+20}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}-6x+10)(x+2).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2=0\\,⟹\\,x=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-2,3\\pm \\text{i}.$",
